    <div>
        <p><br><br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbspBelow is a description of Loyalty and Pride that has been pasted from the Sacred Heart College website. <br><br><br><br><br><i><b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"We are true to our tradition<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and are proud that Sacred Heart College has contributed to the lives of our students, <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;who are justly proud of their Catholic faith, <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;underpinned by our Marist and Champagnat heritage."</b></i><br><br><br><br><br> &nbspTo me loyalty and pride means dedication, honor, trust and honor within a group. <br><br><br><br><br>&nbspIf you are intrested in reading more about Family Spirit then you shoul follow <a href="https://www.sacredheart.school.nz/our-college/special-character">this link</a><br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp<br>&nbsp</p>
    </div>
    <h2>&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbsp&nbspMy Story</h2>
        <img src="/static/Spirit1.JPG">
    <div class=texty>
        <p>My example of Loyalty amd Pride comes from 2025 when I joined the Sacred Heart College Year 9 EPro8 Team, <br>or as we called ourselves: 'The Sacred Circuts'. <br><br><br>EPro8 is an inter-school science and engineering competition in which over 35,000 students across the nation compete.<br><br>EPro8 Stands for:<br><br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<i><b>E</b></i>nginner<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<i><b>Pro</i></b>blem Solve<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Innov|<i><b>8</i></b>|ate<br><br>When I first stepped onto the ship, I felt completely out of my comfort zone and initialy started by just keeping to myself but this quickly changed thanks to the activities, bonding and meeting lots of life long friends.<br><br>The Spirit Of Adventure was a great experience teaching me important leadership skills, communication, and letting me meet more people outside of my normal friend group.<br><br>After the 5-Day voyage, I had created a life-long bond with everyone else on the boat showing me the importance of 'Family Spirit'.</p>
    </div class=texty>
